{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"73c25883e2056bf3e9eb8710c6f31c8169b6920b45908ff0aaae61e9068dc229","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_7495220f8b11b1c76d25b5588291bc09358a9d865c849696b3c52745dad7a7eb","overall_assessment":"The paper presents a technically coherent method for enhancing CNN feature diversity using privileged segmentation information. The experimental design is robust, utilizing standard benchmarks and ablation studies to validate the core claims. However, the lack of statistical significance testing and the omission of code availability details limit the reproducibility and statistical rigor of the reported improvements.","paper_id":"ByQPVFull","paper_identity_sha256":"b9d8e4f9c7ca696c58d739e3407f91c6c6025748760dadceea8ea71d0fe4b846","prompt_identity_sha256":"4dafe4f8f145d6a36d0bc18111df3ae27894b74ac8593df0e69b9173488340a4","raw_response_sha256":"34df411fe751df380de6bda18a7200e54127c30600a8b6052642f33d7493e583","request_identity_sha256":"76001c0bc0b684f53d527d9e81f01e6e569dd64e7ee09fa7b43bf62347550f94","reviewer_identity_sha256":"c1cd7c7fdd4a2cbeb45c2f21af982ad0f30bffae8ae148e3eba36479685cf360","role":"QUAL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"8238af44ccfd707a0688efb7780917a7edf2a669face732be5c6949e0dd6cfae","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-011","SRC-012","SRC-016","SRC-017","SRC-018"],"review_text":"The proposed GoCNN architecture is mathematically well-formulated. The paper defines model diversity and group-wise diversity clearly, providing a logical basis for the optimization objective. The method correctly implements the suppression of background features in the foreground group and vice versa using element-wise multiplication with masks, which is a standard and appropriate technique for spatial feature isolation. The training procedure, which combines classification loss with these suppression terms, is consistent with the stated goal of learning orthogonal feature groups. No conceptual errors or mis-specified objectives are apparent in the methodological description.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-MET"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-021","SRC-022","SRC-025","SRC-028","SRC-030","SRC-033","SRC-035"],"review_text":"The experimental design is comprehensive, evaluating the model on both ImageNet and PASCAL VOC. The authors appropriately use ResNet-18 and ResNet-152 as baselines, which are standard for this era of research. The inclusion of ablation studies (Table 2) effectively isolates the contribution of the foreground and background groups, supporting the claim that both components are necessary for optimal performance. The experiments on partial privileged information (Table 4) further validate the robustness of the method. The use of 10-crop testing for the main results and single-crop for the partial information experiments is a reasonable trade-off between computational cost and evaluation rigor.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-EXP"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-023","SRC-024"],"review_text":"The paper provides sufficient implementation details for reproduction, including the specific hyperparameters for SGD (learning rate, momentum, weight decay), batch sizes, and data augmentation strategies (random cropping and scaling). The choice of base architectures (ResNet-18 and ResNet-152) and the specific dataset splits (ImageNet-0.1m and PASCAL VOC 2012) are clearly defined. However, the paper does not explicitly state whether the code is available or provide a link to a repository, which is a minor gap in reproducibility best practices for this venue.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-REP"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-007","SRC-008","SRC-026"],"review_text":"The paper positions its work well against relevant prior art, specifically comparing against SVM+ (a standard privileged information method) and the vanilla ResNet baseline. The discussion of related work appropriately distinguishes GoCNN from knowledge distillation and DeCov, highlighting the unique use of privileged segmentation masks for group orthogonality. The comparison with SVM+ is particularly relevant as it shares the LUPI paradigm, and the paper correctly notes that GoCNN does not require extra parameters compared to the baseline, ensuring a fair comparison.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-CMP"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-025","SRC-030","SRC-035"],"review_text":"The paper reports mean validation accuracies and error rates but does not provide confidence intervals, standard deviations, or significance tests. Given that the improvements over the baseline are sometimes modest (e.g., 0.71% in Table 4), the absence of statistical validation makes it difficult to determine if these differences are statistically significant or due to random variation in training. The reliance on single-run results for the main comparisons limits the statistical rigor of the conclusions.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-STA"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"57f949d502fce1ac782829577b88d52dbcab0c0afa1063bd2bf693aef336dbf6","paper_id":"ByQPVFull","paper_ordinal":70,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"34df411fe751df380de6bda18a7200e54127c30600a8b6052642f33d7493e583","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"ByQPVFull","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"2dee507fce170feff4bbb48164c95405e21d7b4d9fa339988edbc032b7032184","request_identity_sha256":"76001c0bc0b684f53d527d9e81f01e6e569dd64e7ee09fa7b43bf62347550f94","role":"QUAL","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v5","usage":{"completion_tokens":1026,"prompt_tokens":17222,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":18248},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"76001c0bc0b684f53d527d9e81f01e6e569dd64e7ee09fa7b43bf62347550f94","role":"QUAL","role_ordinal":0,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}